Because mixing angles are large (	heta_{12} \approx 33.7^\circ, 	heta_{23} \approx 49.1^\circ, 	heta_{13} \approx 8.5^\circ), individual flavour states are spread significantly across mass states. For instance, the muon neutrino state \vert{}
u_\muangle = U_{\mu 1}^* \vert{}
u_1angle + U_{\mu 2}^* \vert{}
u_2angle + U_{\mu 3}^* \vert{}
u_3angle has fractional contents:0.236 < \vert{}U_{\mu 1}^*\vert{} < 0.507, \quad 0.458 < \vert{}U_{\mu 2}^*\vert{} < 0.691, \quad 0.630 < \vert{}U_{\mu 3}^*\vert{} < 0.779

Thus, there is no single “mass of a muon neutrino.”

